      "writtenOn": "2026-11-23T20:46:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Lifecycle groups the four states that carry no data, so each can be an enum constant shared by all streams. Failed and Interrupted carry the cause for a particular stream and use it to create a fresh exception on each read or append. The grouping is intentional, but I agree the name is unclear. Lifecycle sounds like it should cover all six states. `NormalState` would make the distinction clearer.",
      "parentUuid": "6562e7a9_c0707e81",
