      "writtenOn": "2026-11-23T15:19:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "why do we need stream id? IIRC when streaming output it was managed internally by Netty?",
      "revId": "d6517acb65eb635561c1d7919017d1e18df048bf",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fdb9601a_fba89942",
        "filename": "transport/transport-http/src/main/java/org/opendaylight/netconf/transport/http/ServerRequestExecutor.java",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 48,
      "author": {
        "id": 9173
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-23T20:46:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, Netty managed it for RESTCONF HTTP/2 response internally. The HTTP/1.1 request-body path has no stream id of its own. streamId was already in RequestContext before this patch. The executor preserves it across asynchronous completion because HTTPServerSession.respond() copies it into the response headers when present. This patch adds only body to the record",
      "parentUuid": "ee8e5b22_bd14dfcb",
      "revId": "d6517acb65eb635561c1d7919017d1e18df048bf",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
    },
